{
  "id": "mozart-effect",
  "term": "Mozart effect",
  "definition": "The Mozart effect refers to the idea that listening to music before starting a cognitive task may influence later performance, in contrast to music played during the task. In this source, it is described as prior-to-task music listening that might change memory performance by reducing distraction, although findings are mixed and often show no benefit in healthy adults.",
